# Whitelist approach: ignore everything by default, then explicitly
# allow only the file types we want tracked for this paper's repo
# (source .tex, compiled .pdf, supporting .py script, and .csv data).
# This keeps LaTeX build artifacts (.aux, .log, .synctex.gz, .out,
# .toc, .fdb_latexmk, .fls, etc.) and any other clutter out of git
# without having to list every possible junk extension by name.

# Ignore everything
*

# But still walk into directories, so allowed files inside
# subfolders (if any get added later) are not skipped
!*/

# Allow only these file types
!*.pdf
!*.tex
!*.py
!*.csv

# Keep this .gitignore itself tracked
!.gitignore
